// EXPECT: E0223 — `%` is not defined on floats (ADR-0040 §7)
// The sign of a float remainder is a language decision Jairs has not taken: C's `fmod`
// truncates toward zero, Python's `%` follows the divisor, and they disagree on
// `-1.0 % 3.0`. Refused with the reason rather than a bare "unsupported".
main :: () {
    a := 1.5;
    b := a % a;
}
